# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the Live tests:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=ninjam/live/tests/tsan.supp ./live_client_test
#
# AOO's lock-free free list of the RT memory pool (a Treiber stack with a
# tagged head, rt_memory_pool.hpp) reads the head node's 'next' field while
# another thread may pop that node and reuse its memory; the
# compare-exchange that follows then fails because the tag changed, and
# the value read is thrown away. rt_memory_pool.hpp says so ("Technically,
# this is UB, but we don't care because the CAS loop will fail anyway").
# To TSan it is a data race, reported from wherever the memory is used next
# (an event, a queue node). Nothing else is suppressed.
race:aoo::detail::free_list::pop
